{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:19:16.848Z","ordinal":23193,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06991-c870-7270-aadf-b83708099407","author":"/root/pr184_remote_race_behavior","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_remote_race_behavior\nPayload:\nComparison complete.\n\n- `d00b2c6e` (local) is better for Python import syntax:\n  - Handles parenthesized, multiline, comments, explicit backslash continuations, malformed continuations, and source-order scanning.\n  - Its parser regression suite passes.\n  - Remote `071afb51` fails these local parser tests:\n    - `TestParenthesizedPythonFromImportKeepsScopedFFIAndImportScannersAligned`\n    - `REDACTED`\n\n- `071afb51` (remote) is better for:\n  - Signature/default/annotation calls — both trees pass the signature suite.\n  - Basic aliased imports — remote passes; local fails parenthesized alias resolution.\n  - C → Objective-C plain declaration compatibility — remote C/ObjC matrix passes; local fails because it lacks the `C -> Objective-C` edge.\n  - Objective-C-only class/selector filtering remains correct in remote.\n\nImportant remote defect: its alias mapping is file-global, not scope/temporal.\n\nRepro on remote:\n\n```python\ndef first(v):\n    from alpha import compute as c\n    return c(v)\n\ndef second(v):\n    from beta import measure as c\n    return c(v)\n```\n\nRemote emits external `alpha.c` / `beta.c` edges instead of resolving `compute` / `measure`. Sequential reimports in one function show the same false-negative behavior. No false positives appeared in these probes, but this is a real loss of valid edges.\n\nRecommendation:\n\n1. Merge `071afb51` normally to retain signature handling, basic alias support, and C/ObjC compatibility.\n2. Manually union in the `d00b2c6e` Python import-statement parser; do not cherry-pick the local commit wholesale.\n3. Replace remote’s global alias-member lookup with per-call scope/temporal alias resolution before approval.\n4. Add regression tests for function-local and sequential alias rebinding.\n\nDo not use an ours merge: it would discard the remote C/alias/signature fixes."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788477556.848}}}
