{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:23:09.909Z","ordinal":23246,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06995-56d5-7172-87a0-f303fbb0d60c","author":"/root/pr184_class_header_scope","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_class_header_scope\nPayload:\nCurrent implementation is wrong.\n\n- Method defaults and eager annotations execute in the class body namespace.\n  - Class-only `from frobnicate import compute` + `def m(self, x=compute(1))` should resolve `compute`.\n  - Current provider emits no `CALLS` relation.\n- A class binding shadows the module import during direct header evaluation.\n  - With module `compute`, then `class C: compute = None; def m(...=compute(1))`, current provider emits a false C call; Python raises `TypeError`.\n\nNested expressions differ:\n\n- Lambda body and comprehension result/filter do not close over class locals; they use enclosing lexical/global lookup.\n- Only a comprehension’s first iterable is evaluated in the surrounding class/header execution scope.\n- Current provider wrongly resolves that first iterable through the module import when class-local `compute` shadows it.\n\nSmallest sound fix:\n\n1. Keep method-body scope parent as `parent.lexicalContainer()`.\n2. Create function header scope with direct `parent = scope` and a `headerEval` marker.\n3. At publish time, resolve calls owned by `headerEval` through its immediate execution parent, including class bindings; keep ordinary lexical lookup unchanged.\n4. In comprehensions, walk only the first iterable in the enclosing/header scope; walk later iterables, filters, and result in the comprehension child scope.\n\nAlso: under `from __future__ import annotations`, annotations are stringized rather than immediately executed; whether to emit static `CALLS` for them is a separate policy choice."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788477789.909127}}}
