{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:23:30.126Z","ordinal":23257,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a0170a21887d09daa2bc341a8c315","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The comparison is decisive: the remote C/Objective-C refinement is correct and independent, so I’m retaining that commit unchanged. The remote Python parser is weaker than ours, and its alias resolver is file-global and loses valid per-function/sequential aliases; those will not be merged verbatim. I’m keeping our reviewed parser and porting only scope-correct alias behavior."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788477808589,"completed_at_ms":1788477810126}}
