{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:30:07.660Z","ordinal":23387,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a0699b-b6ac-7483-8448-e5caf4a424d7","author":"/root/pr184_class_header_scope","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_class_header_scope\nPayload:\nCLEAN.\n\nVerified on the uncommitted patch:\n\n- Direct method defaults and parameter/return annotations resolve through class imports.\n- Method bodies still skip class scope.\n- Nested lambdas plus comprehension result/filter skip class scope.\n- A comprehension’s first iterable retains class-header lookup.\n- Module-level nested defaults retain module bindings.\n- Methods inside a class nested in a function correctly inherit the outer function binding, not the class binding.\n\nPassed:\n\n```text\ngo test ./internal/sem -run 'TestPython(FunctionHeadersUseLexicalImportScope|MethodHeadersUseClassExecutionScopeOnlyWherePythonDoes)$' -count=1 -v\n```\n\nManual provider snapshot also confirmed class-vs-outer-function targets. No edits."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788478207.660709}}}
