{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:49:14.623Z","ordinal":23724,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069ad-36fd-70f2-a6ff-88b60912810e","author":"/root/pr184_alias_semantic_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_semantic_review\nPayload:\nFindings:\n\n1. P1 — Mixed alias contexts discard valid external edges.  \n   `resolvePythonAliasImportTargets` collects both local targets and external relations, but [provider.go:3892](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/provider.go:3892) emits alias externals only when `len(targets) == 0`. Repro: sequential `c` aliases to local `one.one_target` and unresolved `missing.external_target` emit only the local edge; a standalone unresolved alias correctly emits `external:symbol:missing.external_target`. Emit alias externals additively, independent of local alias targets.\n\n2. P1 — Owner/name-level `importBlocked` suppresses legitimate calls and broadens into same-file constructors.  \n   Nested lambdas publish under the enclosing function owner, so a lambda parameter marks `blocked[run][compute]`; [provider.go:3780](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/provider.go:3780) then makes the whole owner/name handled and removes an outer valid imported call. Confirmed failing test: `TestBareImportedCallIgnoresPythonLocalBinding/a_lambda_parameter_does_not_shadow_the_enclosing_body` returns zero CALLS.  \n   Also, [python_scopes.go:443](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:443) walks to module scope and treats ordinary module declarations as import blockers. This suppresses `check_token -> AuthService` construction; confirmed `TestProviderGoldenSnapshots` fails only `python-basic`, missing its `CONSTRUCTS` edge.\n\n   Minimal model: retain `genericAllowed` per owner/name (true if any call can use normal resolution), rather than an aggregate blocked bit. Filter normal import modules to contexts with `member == local`; resolve aliases separately; union targets; emit alias externals independently. Stop `blocksImport` at the real module scope (`parent == nil`) so module classes/functions remain normal same-file candidates. This preserves all-blocked behavior while allowing outer calls beside lambda/comprehension shadows.\n\nChecks run: focused new alias tests passed; existing Python scope tests passed; the lambda regression and Python golden failure reproduced as above."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788479354.621648}}}
