{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:54:27.785Z","ordinal":23812,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069b1-fe48-7b60-818f-23e81e656fe1","author":"/root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review\nPayload:\nAdversarial review findings for PR #184 (all read-only; temporary repro tests removed; worktree retains only the three PR-modified files):\n\n1. **Nested scope state can poison the enclosing function** (initial diff; parent has reproduced/fixed directionally).\n\n   Minimal repro:\n\n   ```python\n   from lib import compute\n\n   def run(x):\n       f = lambda compute: compute(1)\n       return compute(x)\n   ```\n\n   The lambda’s shadowed call was aggregated under `run`, suppressing the valid outer import call. The same occurs with a comprehension or nested class body containing a shadowed call.\n\n2. **Sequential aliases are aggregated, not resolved per call site.**\n\n   ```python\n   def run():\n       from one import first as c\n       c(1)\n       from two import second as c\n       c(2)\n   ```\n\n   Emits both `one.first` and `two.second` from `run`, so each call is effectively linked to both bindings.\n\n3. **Mixed resolved/unresolved aliases drop the unresolved external edge.**\n\n   ```python\n   def run():\n       from one import compute as c\n       c(1)\n       from missing import compute as c\n       c(2)\n   ```\n\n   Only the resolved local edge is emitted; `pythonAliasExternal` is emitted only when the aggregate target list is empty.\n\n4. **`from . import member as alias` and `from .. import ...` fail.**\n\n   `importBindings` stores `\".\"`/`\"..”` as the module and the member separately, but resolution needs `.member`/`..member` to locate the actual file. Runtime repros for same-language, foreign, and parenthesized forms produced no CALLS.\n\n5. **Incomplete parsing loses the original imported member for aliases.**\n\n   ```python\n   from lib import Widget as W\n   ...\n   broken = (\n   ```\n\n   With `lib.py: class Widget`, the fallback emits external `lib.W` instead of preserving `lib.Widget`; cross-language fallback similarly uses the alias spelling.\n\nChecks run after the parent’s intermediate fixes compiled:\n\n```text\ngo test ./internal/sem -run \\\n'TestBareImportedCallIgnoresPythonLocalBinding|TestPythonScopedFromImportAliasesResolveOriginalMember|TestParenthesizedPythonFromImportKeepsScopedFFIAndImportScannersAligned|TestProviderGoldenSnapshots/python-basic|TestLanguageExtractionMatrix/python' \\\n-count=1\n```\n\nAll selected tests passed after the current edits, but the sequential/mixed/relative/incomplete cases above remain actionable review gaps."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788479667.784933}}}
