{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:54:46.446Z","ordinal":23821,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a08c310a487d0bc4972c6476da00e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Luna added two real gaps: relative aliases and malformed-file fallback spelling. One claimed “sequential alias” issue is not a defect in this graph schema—the relation is function-to-target, so a function that calls both bindings should have both edges. I’m fixing the two genuine gaps and keeping that distinction explicit for the trail.\n\nSeparately, the new remote C commit has its own overreach: it lets C resolve a C++ class merely because the class is nested inside an `extern \"C\"` block. That exact repro fails, so I’m reviewing a kind-level guard before retaining the commit."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788479683009,"completed_at_ms":1788479686446}}
