{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:58:49.832Z","ordinal":23896,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069b5-fde8-7a63-b3ba-a10d60ad5cbc","author":"/root/pr184_alias_semantic_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_semantic_review\nPayload:\nP1 — `cLinkage` is too broad: it marks every declaration lexically under `extern \"C\"` as C-reachable.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- Existing `zz_pr184_review_test.go` fails: C resolves `Hidden` (`class`) for both `USES_TYPE` and `PARAM_TYPE`.\n- A focused matrix also incorrectly resolves:\n  - `struct MethodHolder { int method() {...}; }` (C++ member syntax)\n  - `enum class ScopedEnum`\n  - `namespace nested { struct Namespaced {...}; }`\n- It retains intended C-compatible declarations: plain `struct`, unscoped `enum`, C `typedef`, and ordinary function.\n- `TestCNamesOnlyExternCDeclarationsInCPlusPlusHeaders` and `TestProviderGoldenSnapshots` pass, so do not restore the removed `extern \"C\"` masking.\n\nFix direction:\n\n- Make `Entity.cLinkage` mean “C-compatible declaration within `extern \"C\"`,” not merely lexical containment.\n- At [parser.go:3914](/tmp/entire-graph-pr184-a09.s64Y8r/internal/sem/parser.go:3914), combine linkage ancestry with a parser-level compatibility guard.\n- Reject declarations with a class or namespace ancestor before the linkage specification; reject `class`, `enum class`/`enum struct`, and `using` aliases; reject structs/unions containing C++ members/access specifiers.\n- Preserve ordinary C-style structs/unions, unscoped enums, C typedefs, and C-compatible function declarations.\n- Keep [langcompat.go:221](/tmp/entire-graph-pr184-a09.s64Y8r/internal/sem/langcompat.go:221) as `return candidate.cLinkage`; the flag’s producer needs narrowing.\n\nFocused tests:\n\n- `go test ./internal/sem -run '^TestReviewCDoesNotNameCPlusPlusClassInsideExternC$' -count=1` — currently fails.\n- Extend the linkage fixture with namespace, C++ member-struct, scoped enum, and `using` alias negatives; retain plain struct/function/typedef positives.\n- `go test ./internal/sem -run '^TestCNamesOnlyExternCDeclarationsInCPlusPlusHeaders$|^TestProviderGoldenSnapshots$' -count=1` — currently passes."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788479929.832151}}}
