{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:02:39.413Z","ordinal":23978,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069b9-7eb5-7140-9fd2-d691738b34a3","author":"/root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review\nPayload:\nNew actionable finding:\n\n- **Incomplete top-level aliased imports lose their external fallback.**\n\n  Repro:\n\n  ```python\n  from one import compute as c\n  c(1)\n  broken = (\n  ```\n\n  With `one.c` defining `compute`, the updated code emits no CALLS relation at all. The per-symbol path correctly emits `external:symbol:one.compute`, but the top-level path only sets `pythonGenericAllowed = false` for `pythonIncompleteAliases[name]` and never populates/emits `pythonAliasExternal`.\n\n  Fix: mirror the per-symbol incomplete branch by deriving and emitting `pythonAliasExternalCallRelations(fileSource, pythonIncompleteAliases[name])` in the top-level loop.\n\nChecks:\n\n- `TestPythonScopedAliasesComposeWithGenericResolution`: pass\n- `TestPythonScopedFromImportAliasesResolveOriginalMember`: pass\n- `TestParenthesizedPythonFromImportKeepsScopedFFIAndImportScannersAligned`: pass\n- `TestPythonBareImportFFIRespectsASTScopes`: still fails the already-known plain dotted-import-root regression (`import frobnicate.extra`; expected `importModules` to retain `frobnicate.extra`).\n- Temporary repro removed; no changes remain beyond the PR diff."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788480159.413414}}}
