{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:12:01.609Z","ordinal":24191,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069c2-12c9-72a0-aaab-4f9c4254b974","author":"/root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review\nPayload:\nActionable findings; do not cherry-pick `20d89c01` wholesale.\n\n- The current local scope walker still has the try/with bug:\n  - `except_clause` uses nonexistent `body`/`name` fields and returns early, so exception expressions and handler calls are omitted.\n  - `with_item` uses nonexistent `alias`; function-wide collection recursively treats the whole `as_pattern` (including the context expression) as bindings.\n  - Minimal current repros showed missing FFI CALLS for `except compute():`, handler-body `compute()`, try-body+handler calls, and `with compute() as handle`.\n  - Smallest port: manually apply only the remote `asPatternAlias`, `except_clause`/`except_group_clause`, `with_item`, and `as_pattern_target` changes in `python_scopes.go`.\n\n- The current parser still consumes the rest of the file after an unclosed parenthesized `from` import:\n\n  ```python\n  from broken import (\n      thing,\n  from mod import helper\n  ```\n\n  `importedPythonNames(content)[\"helper\"]` is empty. Port the remote commit’s bounded/no-consume behavior into the current `pythonFromImportStatements`; do not replace the current parser with the remote’s obsolete line-oriented scanner.\n\nAlready handled locally:\n\n- Comprehension outermost iterable semantics are present (`outermost` uses the parent scope).\n- Closed multiline/parenthesized imports are handled by the current `pythonFromImportStatements`.\n- Existing alias, mixed local/external, relative, constructor, and incomplete top-level tests pass.\n\nCherry-pick assessment:\n\n```text\ngit apply --check <(git diff --binary a09defd6 20d89c01)\n```\n\nconflicts in `call_resolution_precision_test.go`, `provider.go`, and `python_scopes.go`; only `provider_test.go` applies cleanly. The provider scanner hunk is obsolete against the current two-result `importedPythonNamesAndForms`/shared parser, and blindly taking the remote comprehension hunk would regress local outermost-iterable behavior. Temporary repro files were removed; no review changes remain."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788480721.609273}}}
