{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:17:43.622Z","ordinal":24317,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a0e26103c87d0ade434eb4fcd7bf9","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The C guard is now narrowed without remasking `extern \"C\"`: plain structs/unions/enums/typedefs/functions stay visible to C; classes, method-bearing aggregates, scoped enums, aliases, namespace members, and other C++ syntax do not. Its focused tests are green. The only remaining local fix is the malformed multiline-import cursor bug, which is a bounded parser-loop change."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788481062017,"completed_at_ms":1788481063622}}
