{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:19:15.198Z","ordinal":24344,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a0e82664087d086b5cd38df5ea23e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The first post-fix review is clean. I caught two issues in the C guard before accepting it: it was reparsing every C/C++ aggregate instead of only `extern \"C\"` candidates, and nested `extern \"C++\"` could inherit an outer C linkage incorrectly. Those are being corrected with an innermost-linkage rule and a regression test."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788481154307,"completed_at_ms":1788481155198}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:19:15.201Z","ordinal":24345,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a0e82664087d086b5cd38df5ea23e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The first post-fix review is clean. I caught two issues in the C guard before accepting it: it was reparsing every C/C++ aggregate instead of only `extern \"C\"` candidates, and nested `extern \"C++\"` could inherit an outer C linkage incorrectly. Those are being corrected with an innermost-linkage rule and a regression test."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
