{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:31:36.487Z","ordinal":24540,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069d4-0027-71b1-b593-03f4bae291be","author":"/root/pr184_alias_semantic_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_semantic_review\nPayload:\nP1 — multiline/commented scoped enums bypass the C-compatibility filter.\n\n`cxxScopedEnum` only matches literal `\"enum class\"` / `\"enum struct\"`. Valid:\n\n```cpp\nextern \"C\" {\nenum\nclass Scoped { One };\n}\n```\n\ncurrently produces `USES_TYPE` and `PARAM_TYPE` from C to `C++/Scoped`.\n\nUse comment-stripped tokens rather than literal prefixes, e.g. `strings.Fields(stripCodeLiteralsAndComments(node.Content(src)))`. Keep the existing ancestor and aggregate-member guards; a C-parser oracle alone cannot replace them because methods and namespaced functions can parse as standalone C declarations, and syntax parsing has no typedef/class symbol knowledge.\n\nFocused existing linkage, golden, and stable-ID tests pass."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788481896.487576}}}
