{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:37:12.296Z","ordinal":24629,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069d9-1fe8-7c82-a034-84993a20a54e","author":"/root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_adversarial_review\nPayload:\nActionable finding: `cxxAggregateMembers` misses C++-only members that Tree-sitter’s C grammar accepts without errors.\n\nMinimal repro:\n\n```cpp\nextern \"C\" {\n  struct Outer { struct Inner { int x; }; };\n  struct StaticMember { static int x; };\n}\n```\n\nCurrent parser marks `Outer`, nested `Inner`, and `StaticMember` as `cLinkage=true`. `Inner` is a nested C++ type unavailable to C, while `static` data members are invalid C struct members. The explicit-member walk only rejects methods/templates/access specifiers and does not inspect nested aggregate declarations or storage-class members.\n\nFocused existing C-linkage tests pass, including nested `extern \"C++\"`, scoped enums with comments/newlines, aliases, plain function-pointer fields, namespace/class descendants, and method exclusions. Temporary repro was removed; `git diff --check` is clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788482232.296745}}}
