{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:44:10.542Z","ordinal":24737,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069df-81ae-7180-ad95-b7dcf0480523","author":"/root/pr184_alias_semantic_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_alias_semantic_review\nPayload:\nP1 — `cxxNestedAggregateWithoutField` suppresses valid C11 anonymous aggregate members.\n\n`struct AnonymousOuter { struct { int value; }; };` compiles with `cc -std=c11`, but the new no-declarator guard marks it C++-only. A C caller consequently emits no `USES_TYPE`/`PARAM_TYPE` edge to `AnonymousOuter`; the function-pointer control still resolves.\n\nThe syntax is indistinguishable from a C++ nested declaration at this node granularity, so absence of `declarator` cannot be a safe C-compatibility rejection. Remove/narrow that guard and rely on the bounded C-parser compatibility check (plus unambiguous C++ forms). Add an anonymous `struct` and `union` member fixture with C consumers; retain named nested aggregate and function-pointer positives. The existing focused linkage test passes."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788482650.542621}}}
