{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:47:29.338Z","ordinal":24802,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a151f949487d0a9dbfddbfbf679ab","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Both C reviewers are now clean, and that correction is committed. The remote branch moved again during review with two new Trail-driven fixes:\n\n- Python definition names becoming visible too early in their own signatures;\n- Objective-C access to the C-compatible half of `extern \"C\"` C++ headers.\n\nI’m comparing both against our exact head in parallel; the shared C-compatibility guard should make the second one cheap to retain safely."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788482847481,"completed_at_ms":1788482849338}}
