{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:53:17.032Z","ordinal":24894,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a167b878487d0bf6ab4bd22e3713d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The Python definition-timing issue is confirmed: defaults, annotations, class bases, and class-body expressions must see the old enclosing name; recursive function/method bodies must see the newly bound definition. The port is isolated to the existing scope model, not the remote commit’s older parser code. After it lands, the Objective-C extension is a one-condition change plus fixture coverage."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788483195397,"completed_at_ms":1788483197032}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:53:17.036Z","ordinal":24895,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a167b878487d0bf6ab4bd22e3713d","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The Python definition-timing issue is confirmed: defaults, annotations, class bases, and class-body expressions must see the old enclosing name; recursive function/method bodies must see the newly bound definition. The port is isolated to the existing scope model, not the remote commit’s older parser code. After it lands, the Objective-C extension is a one-condition change plus fixture coverage."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
