{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:58:27.245Z","ordinal":25008,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a069ec-942c-75b1-8a8c-39efe63fd86c","author":"/root/pr184_c_linkage_finish","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr184_c_linkage_finish\nPayload:\nImplemented the Objective-C extern-C extension without changing `typeSharingLanguageEdges` or touching Luna’s files.\n\nDiff:\n- `candidateSharesDeclarations` now uses a small helper for C and Objective-C consumers of C++-labelled candidates, returning true only when `candidate.cLinkage` is set.\n- Objective-C++ remains excluded from that exception and continues through normal C++ sharing.\n- Extended `TestCNamesOnlyExternCDeclarationsInCPlusPlusHeaders` with a `.m` consumer:\n  - Objective-C → C controls pass.\n  - Objective-C → C++ `extern \"C\"` struct/function edges resolve.\n  - C++ class, namespace function, and overload candidates remain excluded.\n\nSelf-review: the helper is restricted to exactly `\"C\"` and `\"Objective-C\"`; no language-level C++ edge was added, and all Objective-C positives still depend on the existing per-declaration `cLinkage` flag.\n\nVerified:\n\n- `gofmt -w internal/sem/langcompat.go internal/sem/langcompat_test.go`\n- `go test ./internal/sem -run '^(TestObjectiveC.*|TestCNamesOnly.*|TestLanguagesShareTypesRelation|TestTypeReferenceKeepsSharedDeclarationLanguages)$' -count=1`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNo commit or push."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788483507.244989}}}
