{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:23:18.369Z","ordinal":25490,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a03-54e1-7d51-b469-bc53bdd563bc","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\n**P1 — `deferredParent` is not consumed by lambda or generator bodies.**\n\nIt is assigned in [walkComprehension](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:413) but only read by [preDefinitionView](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:655). Neither the lambda path nor the generator’s completed-boundary path consults it.\n\nConsequently, both deferred forms nested inside an eager method-header comprehension retain the pre-class chain:\n\n```python\nfrom frobnicate import compute\n\nclass compute:\n    def method(self, value=[lambda: compute() for _ in range(1)]):\n        return value\n```\n\nand\n\n```python\nfrom frobnicate import compute\n\nclass compute:\n    def method(self, value=[(compute() for _ in range(1)) for _ in range(1)]):\n        return value\n```\n\nCPython confirms both deferred calls resolve the completed class when invoked/iterated. The walker instead reaches the import because the header comprehension’s parent is deliberately pre-class and the `deferredParent` hint is unused. Add separate method-owner regressions expecting no imported `compute` modules.\n\nAlso, [preDefinitionView](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:655) can return early without hiding the class’s own synthetic binding when `deferredParent` is set. That branch is presently hard to reach with valid Python syntax (only comprehension scopes get the field), but it violates the helper’s contract and is not the mechanism needed for lambda/generator deferral.\n\nThe existing focused test passes but does not exercise either method-header deferred case."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788484998.369496}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:23:30.696Z","ordinal":25491,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_064395e280df5569016a9a1d89833087d0b65fe75daabfc78e","summary_text":["**Deciding deferredParent usage and naming**","**Designing deferredNestedParent method**"],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1788485001344,"completed_at_ms":1788485010696}}
