{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:23:36.736Z","ordinal":25495,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a1d973e7887d0b8b28dcc9afce86a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Terra confirmed the last implementation carried the alternate parent but never used it; it also added an unreachable early return that violated the class-view contract. I’m replacing that plumbing with one explicit rule: eager comprehension uses its immediate parent, while a deferred child receives an alternate copy of the same comprehension scope with only the class boundary switched. That preserves loop variables and avoids special-case leakage."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788485015135,"completed_at_ms":1788485016736}}
