{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:27:44.938Z","ordinal":25583,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a07-662a-7620-b1b3-1d5999c51201","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\n**P2 — the two new method-header deferred paths have no regression tests.**\n\nThe implementation is now correct by source trace:\n\n- A lambda inside the eager header list comprehension calls `deferredNestedParent()`, which preserves comprehension bindings and swaps its pre-class parent for the completed scope.\n- A nested generator uses that same completed cloned comprehension scope for its deferred clauses/body, while its first iterable remains evaluated through the original eager parent.\n- `preDefinitionView` now always installs the class-event hide.\n\nCPython confirms both required semantics, and the focused definition test passes. However, [call_resolution_precision_test.go:758](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/call_resolution_precision_test.go:758) covers only the eager method-header list-comprehension call; it has no assertions for:\n\n```python\nclass compute:\n    def method(self, value=[lambda: compute() for _ in range(1)]): ...\n```\n\nor:\n\n```python\nclass compute:\n    def method(self, value=[(compute() for _ in range(1)) for _ in range(1)]): ...\n```\n\nBoth should assert no imported `compute` module. This is the exact new `deferredParent` behavior and needs pinning."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788485264.938179}}}
