{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:30:57.336Z","ordinal":25697,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a0a-55b8-7180-816e-621b62cfc2b5","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\nRecommendation: **port the lambda-default fix, but not as a cherry-pick.**\n\nLocal `ab6a67b4` still walks only lambda bodies, so calls in defaults are absent from the scoped import model. That drops resolution for cases such as:\n\n```python\nfrom frobnicate import compute\ndef plain():\n    return (lambda value=compute(): value)()\n```\n\nCPython confirms defaults use the enclosing scope and do not see sibling lambda parameters; defaults inside a comprehension capture that comprehension’s binding.\n\nRemote `4508c119` fixes the right behavior by walking every non-body lambda child against the original enclosing `scope`, then retaining the isolated child scope for the body. Its regression tests are well targeted: function/module defaults, self-name parameter, body shadowing, local shadowing, and comprehension capture.\n\nDo **not** apply the remote lambda-parent change wholesale: it creates the body child with `scope`, while local `ab6a67b4` correctly requires `scope.deferredNestedParent()` for deferred lambda bodies in/under class construction. A wholesale cherry-pick would regress the local class-timing fixes.\n\nSmall local port in [python_scopes.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go):\n- Keep `child := newPythonBindingScope(scope.owner, scope.deferredNestedParent())`.\n- Before collecting/walking the body, walk each named lambda child other than `body` with the original `scope`.\n- Then retain the existing parameter collection and body walk.\n\nPort remote `TestPythonLambdaDefaultsResolveThroughEnclosingImports`, and add two local integration cases:\n- class-body lambda default resolves the pre-class import;\n- method-header lambda default resolves the pre-class import while its deferred body sees the completed class.\n\nFocused local definition-timing test passes; the remote behavior is currently missing rather than already covered."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788485457.336555}}}
