{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:32:24.320Z","ordinal":25723,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a0b-a980-7c10-8040-be5bae83fcfb","author":"/root/pr188_final_luna","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_luna\nPayload:\nComparison result:\n\n- The only missing behavior in local `HEAD` is `from mod import(item)`.\n- Tab forms already work locally:\n  - `from mod\\timport\\titem`\n  - `from\\tmod\\timport\\titem`\n  - This is because the shared regex allows `\\s+` before `import` and `[ \\t]+` after it.\n- Parenthesized imports with a space also work: `from mod import (item)`.\n- The no-space parenthesized form fails because local `pythonFromImportRE` requires either end-of-input or whitespace after `import`; it cannot consume the following `(`.\n\nRemote commit `9b60f3d1` fixes the AST parser by locating `import` via identifier boundaries. Its boundary logic correctly avoids splitting `importlib`, handles tabs and `import(`, and protects UTF-8 identifier bytes.\n\nRecommendation: port the keyword-boundary logic into the existing shared `pythonFromImportParts`, preserving the shared parser’s full-line/`from` anchoring. Do not copy the remote helper verbatim without that anchoring: as written, it blindly strips a `from` prefix and is safe only because the AST caller guarantees an `import_from_statement`. Add shared-parser tests for:\n\n- `from mod import(item)` (the actual missing case)\n- existing tab forms, to lock them in\n- `from importlib import item`, to prevent keyword splitting\n- ideally a star import and parenthesized multiline form as negative/coverage guards.\n\nNo edits were made."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788485544.320582}}}
