{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:58:35.132Z","ordinal":26099,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a23-a17c-7e43-afdc-4936d79698ae","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\nP1 — port both commits, but do not cherry-pick `98ae8a07` unchanged.\n\n- Local HEAD still binds assignment targets before walking their value at [python_scopes.go:360](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:360), and walrus targets before their value at [python_scopes.go:379](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:379). Thus module-scope `compute = compute()`, `compute += compute()`, destructuring/chained variants, `for compute in compute()`, and `compute := compute()` wrongly suppress the pre-existing import.\n\n  `98ae8a07`’s `addTargetFrom(..., EndByte)` / delayed loop-body binding is the right core model. `cf224577` correctly applies it to `named_expression`, including comprehension hoisting through `walrusScope`; function and lambda cases remain correctly fail-closed through the existing function-wide-local pass.\n\n- However, `98ae8a07` incorrectly treats a bare annotated assignment as a rebinding:\n\n  ```python\n  compute = imported_callable\n  compute: int\n  compute()  # still calls imported_callable\n  ```\n\n  CPython confirms the import remains bound. Its unconditional delayed target registration for `annotated_assignment` would suppress the later import edge. Only register an annotated-assignment target when it has a `right`/value child; retain `collectFunctionBindings` behavior so `compute: int` remains a function-local declaration inside a function.\n\n- Local HEAD has no match/case capture collection in `collectFunctionBindings` ([python_scopes.go:736](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:736)), so `case compute:` does not make `compute` function-local. Port `98ae8a07`’s selective `collectCaseCaptures` logic: its pattern discrimination is sound for bare/as/star/sequence/mapping-value/class positional captures and preserves class names, keyword labels, mapping keys, dotted values, and `_` as loads/non-captures.\n\nP1 follow-up — the remote case port is incomplete at module scope. It only marks function-wide `locals`; it creates no ordered capture event. Consequently these valid semantics remain modeled incorrectly:\n\n```python\nmatch value:\n    case compute:\n        pass\ncompute()                 # compute is now the capture, not the import\n\nmatch value:\n    case compute if compute():\n        pass              # guard sees captured compute, not the import\n```\n\nCPython confirms both. Add ordered capture events for module/class executable scopes, effective after the pattern and before guard/body; retain function-wide local collection for functions.\n\nMinimal implementation/test spec:\n\n1. Add `addTargetFrom`, delay `assignment`/`augmented_assignment` targets to statement end and `for` targets to body start.\n2. Handle `annotated_assignment` separately: delay only when a value exists.\n3. Delay walrus target to named-expression end, retaining `walrusScope`.\n4. Port selective function capture collection.\n5. Add module-level case-capture events at pattern completion.\n6. Tests: RHS self-reference, chained/destructuring, augmented, valued vs valueless annotations, function-local negatives, guard/post-case module negatives, and existing walrus direct/later-expression/comprehension/lambda cases.\n\nCPython oracles verified normal/annotated assignment timing, match capture/guard binding, function-wide capture locality, and walrus value-before-store behavior."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788487115.132206}}}
