{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T02:42:40.424Z","ordinal":26697,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a4b-fea8-70c0-9bb9-7b8b2efadfe9","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\nFindings:\n\n1. P1 — `python-basic` golden exposes a real regression, not a golden update.\n\n`TestProviderGoldenSnapshots/python-basic` drops only:\n\n`check_token -> AuthService.validate` (`DATA_FLOWS`)\n\nOutput falls from 11 to 10 relations. The cause is `genericCallAllowed` returning false for absent scope entries; data-flow reduces `service.validate(token)` to `validate`, but no bare `validate()` call is recorded. Resolution is skipped at [provider.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/provider.go:4065).\n\nSmallest fix: make [genericCallAllowed](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/python_scopes.go:118) return true when the owner/name key is absent. Preserve false for an explicitly recorded alias/module/rebinding case. Keep the existing golden unchanged.\n\n2. P1 — remote `95ac9aaf` fixes a remaining plain-import comment bug.\n\nCurrent [importedPythonNamesAndForms](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/provider.go:20684) and [importedPythonBindings](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/provider.go:23701) parse:\n\n```python\nimport frobnicate as m  # noqa\n```\n\nwith the comment attached, losing alias `m`. This can drop or misresolve `m.compute()`.\n\nPort only the comment stripping for direct `import` branches; do not replace the newer shared `from` parser. Current `from ... import` parsing already strips comments, including parenthesized and valid backslash continuations. Add a focused alias/form/binding plus dotted-call equivalence test.\n\nThe two issues are independent: porting `95ac9aaf` will not fix the golden regression.\n\nChecks run: required `entire graph commit 95ac9aaf --json`; focused from-import tests passed; `git diff --check` and `gofmt -d` clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788489760.424183}}}
