{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:18:41.402Z","ordinal":27147,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a6c-f7fa-78e3-af47-b00764bba40e","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\nPrioritized findings:\n\n1. `43efb16d` improves the local renamed-`@objc` fix.\n\nLocal fail-closes all `@objc(...)`, including valid no-op exports such as `@objc(Same) class Same` and matching selectors. Port its exported-name comparison, but use whitespace-tolerant `@objc\\s*\\(([^)]*)\\)`. This retains fail-close for renamed symbols while preserving same-name exports.\n\n2. `fdf4a86e` fixes a real direct-import bug.\n\nCurrent `import frobnicate as m; x = 1` loses `m` in both direct import consumers, breaking forms/bindings and dotted calls. Port a shared direct-import terminator helper that cuts at the first `#` or `;`; leave `from` parsing unchanged.\n\nAdd an FFI regression with `import frobnicate as m; m.compute(1)` against `frobnicate.c`, plus parser maps/forms/bindings and comment/semicolon ordering checks.\n\nFocused existing tests pass."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788491921.402334}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:18:45.932Z","ordinal":27148,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_064395e280df5569016a9a3893088c87d0846133ad2a0d23e2","summary_text":[],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1788491923001,"completed_at_ms":1788491925932}}
