{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:29:51.231Z","ordinal":27269,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a77-307f-7d91-8ebb-d45fc5458c93","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\nP1 finding: [langcompat.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/.entire/worktrees/pr184-review/internal/sem/langcompat.go:343) matches `@objc(...)` anywhere in a Swift signature.\n\nA valid method such as:\n\n```swift\nfunc f(_ x: String = \"@objc(RenamedThing)\") {}\n```\n\nis incorrectly treated as renamed and hidden from Objective-C. Parameter defaults are part of the captured signature.\n\nConstrain custom-attribute parsing to the leading declaration attribute list; add a literal-default regression. All current focused tests, `^TestPython`, diff, and formatting checks pass, but do not cover this case."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788492591.23101}}}
