{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:38:29.698Z","ordinal":27370,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a7f-19c2-75e1-86d6-de08d31cbb6f","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\nFound blocking scanner issues:\n\n- P1 `langcompat.go:400`: qualified leading attributes are not consumed. Valid Swift `@MyModule.MyAttribute @objc(RenamedThing) class Renamed...` causes the later renamed `@objc` to be accepted by the fallback regex.\n- P1 `langcompat.go:438`: attribute skipping mishandles raw strings and comments containing `)`. Valid examples:\n  - `@MyAttr(#\"x\" ) still raw\"#) @objc(RenamedThing) class Renamed...`\n  - `@MyAttr(/* ) */ value) @objc(RenamedThing) class Renamed...`\n  Both prematurely end the preceding attribute and overexpose the renamed Swift symbol.\n- P1 `langcompat.go:341,369`: the fallback `swiftObjCExposureAttributeRe` remains unanchored. A parameter default/body/comment containing `@objc(...)` makes a global Swift function appear ObjC-visible. The new tests currently assert that incorrect `true` result.\n\nThe balanced leading-attribute approach is proportionate once it handles dotted attribute names, raw-string delimiters, and comments; I would not simplify it to a regex.\n\nDirect Python import terminator change looks correct. `git diff --check`, `gofmt -d`, focused Swift/direct-import tests, and `go test ./internal/sem -run '^TestPython' -count=1` all passed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788493109.698379}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:38:37.976Z","ordinal":27371,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_064395e280df5569016a9a3d39288087d0b2dc9b3ecec97d2f","summary_text":["**Planning precise scanner fixes**"],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1788493113088,"completed_at_ms":1788493117976}}
