{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:45:43.726Z","ordinal":27461,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0616d-0c18-7443-82f2-b4c5bc498542","turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_064395e280df5569016a9a3ee5fa7487d0bc388cd5148ee421","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Terra agrees the 179-line mini-lexer is overbuilt and still has an escaped-string bug. We’re replacing it with a 60–80-line fail-closed prefix parser: support normal `@objc` cases and ordinary `@available`, but return “uncertain → not visible” for exotic or malformed attribute prefixes. That is cheaper and aligned with this PR’s no-false-edge goal."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788493542028,"completed_at_ms":1788493543726}}
