{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:08:49.034Z","ordinal":27718,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a06a9a-dc8a-77c2-ad45-c680cca72ddf","author":"/root/pr188_final_terra","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr188_final_terra\nPayload:\n`bf88d09f` is test-only: it changes only `call_resolution_precision_test.go` and `provider_test.go`.\n\nCoverage mapping:\n\n- Multiline `from` imports, alias binding, comments, malformed-list recovery: locally covered by `TestPythonScopedFromImportAliasesResolveOriginalMember`, `TestParenthesizedPythonFromImportKeepsScopedFFIAndImportScannersAligned`, `TestPythonFromImportKeywordBoundaryForms`, and malformed-list tests.\n- Plain CALLS alias resolution, module-only aliases, local scope, ambiguity: locally covered by `TestPythonScopedFromImportAliasesResolveOriginalMember` and related FFI tests.\n- Direct-import comments/semicolon termination: locally covered by the two new direct-import tests.\n\nGenuine missing coverage:\n\n- `ASYNC_CALLS` and `DATA_FLOWS` parity for `from ... import compute as c`, including ambiguity, module-alias suppression, and function-local non-leak.\n- A `from ... import compute as c  # comment` integration assertion across relation types. Existing comment coverage is only direct `import module as alias`.\n\nRecommendation: test-only minimal port of remote `TestAsyncAndFlowAliasedImportedCallsResolveToTheirOriginalName` plus `relationsTouching`, and a compact from-import-comment alias regression. Do not port the redundant broad CALLS and multiline tests.\n\nCurrent equivalent focused tests and `^TestPython` pass."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0690a-a093-7352-9a6c-ed6ea1d6d3c0","create_time":1788494929.034338}}}
